.TH CSVTUI 1 "2026-08-06" "csvtui 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
csvtui \- terminal viewer for CSV files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B csvtui
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile.csv\fR
.br
\fIcommand\fR | \fBcsvtui\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B csvtui
displays a CSV file as an aligned grid in the terminal and lets you move around
it with vim-style keys. The file is read lazily, so only a window of rows is
resident in memory at any time.
.PP
Quoted fields containing the delimiter or newlines, escaped double quotes,
CRLF line endings and a leading byte order mark are all handled. Column widths
are measured in terminal cells, so accented and double-width text aligns.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delimiter " " \fIchar\fR
Field delimiter. Accepts \fBtab\fR or \fB\\t\fR for tab-separated files.
Auto-detected from the first line when not given.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-header
Treat the first row as data rather than as column names.
.TP
.B \-\-header
Force the first row to be a header. This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B h j k l
Move the cursor. Arrow keys work too.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-D ", " Ctrl\-U
Half page down or up.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-F ", " Ctrl\-B ", " PgDn ", " PgUp
Full page down or up.
.TP
.BR gg ", " G
Jump to the first or last row. \fIn\fBG\fR jumps to row \fIn\fR.
.TP
.BR 0 ", " $
First or last column.
.TP
.B /
Search forward. Search is smart case: an all-lowercase pattern matches
case-insensitively. Searches wrap around the end of the file.
.TP
.BR n ", " N
Next or previous match.
.TP
.B f
Filter rows to those matching a pattern. An empty pattern clears the filter.
.TP
.BR s ", " S
Sort by the cursor column, ascending or descending. Numeric columns sort
numerically.
.TP
.B u
Clear the sort and the filter.
.TP
.BR x ", " X
Hide the cursor column, or show all columns again.
.TP
.B z
Freeze the columns up to the cursor so they stay visible when scrolling right.
.TP
.B Enter
Show the full value of the current cell.
.TP
.B y
Copy the current cell to the system clipboard using OSC 52, which works over
SSH.
.TP
.B c
Show statistics for the cursor column: row count, empty count, and min, max and
mean for numeric columns.
.TP
.B H
Pin or unpin the header row.
.TP
.B t
Toggle between aligned and raw modes.
.TP
.B ?
Toggle the help overlay.
.TP
.B q
Quit. \fBEsc\fR closes an overlay first, and clears the search highlight.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The file could not be read.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH NOTES
Sorting and filtering build an index over the whole file and therefore require
one full pass before the first result appears. All other operations stream.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR column (1),
.BR csvlook (1)
